WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.926
If a dishwasher problem survives one conversation the evidence should

00:00:03.926 --> 00:00:09.027
too FixProof keeps the symptom the source and the user's confirmed outcomes

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:11.717
together Here's the current six-path build

00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:17.103
I'll start a fictional drying case and ask what to check first FixProof

00:00:17.103 --> 00:00:21.286
suggests waiting for drying to finish then links directly to page forty-one

00:00:21.286 --> 00:00:26.150
of the manufacturer's manual The model chooses a bounded check The application

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.982
owns the instruction and citation

00:00:28.998 --> 00:00:33.186
Here's the key rule A suggestion is not evidence that someone performed

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:37.773
a check The user records what actually happened In this fictional case

00:00:38.023 --> 00:00:42.448
the glasses remain wet after thirty minutes That outcome is saved but

00:00:42.448 --> 00:00:44.286
the problem is not declared fixed

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.258
Now reload and resume The observation is still here Ask what to check

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:54.144
next and FixProof moves to rinse aid instead of repeating the recorded

00:00:54.144 --> 00:00:57.040
check The case changes the next interaction

00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:02.078
The current release goes beyond one scripted symptom It maps nineteen

00:01:02.078 --> 00:01:05.478
source-backed checks across six issue paths and three exact dishwasher

00:01:05.478 --> 00:01:10.028
models Each catalog stays separate and every supported step points back

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:11.891
to that model's official manual page

00:01:12.924 --> 00:01:17.286
The handover carries the exact model the recorded outcome the observation

00:01:17.449 --> 00:01:21.911
and the source page It also states what is still unknown Someone can

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:25.299
pick up the case without treating an assistant's suggestion as a fact

00:01:26.342 --> 00:01:30.767
If a burning smell is reported troubleshooting stops The pending check

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:35.342
disappears the warning remains after reload and the original report stays

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:38.367
in the handover No diagnosis is invented

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.831
Judges can call the public M C P endpoint directly An official client

00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:47.655
discovered five tools and all six supported paths preserved the fictional

00:01:47.655 --> 00:01:51.442
case across new connections avoided repeating the recorded check and

00:01:51.442 --> 00:01:55.539
returned the selected model's exact source pages The endpoint and evidence

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:56.900
are linked from the live site

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:02.539
FixProof has not run on an Alexa device or proven a repair outcome It

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:06.377
does demonstrate a narrower result across three exact models and six

00:02:06.377 --> 00:02:10.569
sourced paths a stateful assistant can keep user-confirmed evidence intact

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.117
So the next repair conversation does not start from zero